# No Emojis

Do not use emojis anywhere in this repository or in assistant output for this project.

## Applies to

- Source code, comments, docstrings, and log messages
- Markdown, README, runbooks, architecture docs, and diagrams text
- Commit messages, PR titles, PR bodies, and release notes
- User-facing assistant replies, summaries, and checklists

## Forbidden examples

- Pictograph emojis (faces, objects, symbols with color)
- Status substitutes: checkmark emoji, X mark emoji, warning emoji, rocket, etc.
- Text stand-ins used as icons: heavy check mark, ballot box, cross mark
- GitHub/Slack shortcodes such as `:white_check_mark:` or `:x:`

## Use instead

- Plain words: `Done`, `Failed`, `Warning`, `Note`, `Optional`
- Markdown lists and headings without icon prefixes
- `PASS` / `FAIL`, `Yes` / `No`, `[x]` / `[ ]` only when a checkbox list is required
- ASCII arrows when needed: `->`, not Unicode arrow or emoji arrows

## When editing existing files

- Remove emojis when you touch a file for another reason; do not run repo-wide emoji-only sweeps unless asked.
